*> Registry Data builders (docs/protocol/03 0x07, 04 §3, §4, §6; 09 §3.1, §3.4 rule 9): one packet per
*> registry of core/copy/REGISTRY.cpy that has entries (standin-content §4.2: 18 packets, 52 entries);
*> an empty registry (§4.9) gets no packet. Every entry is sent with Data present (Select Known Packs
*> is empty, standin §4.1) as a network NBT Compound (07 §3) whose fields follow the standin table
*> order (09 §3.4 rule 9). Fields standin gives as absent are not written; real numbers are the
*> table's thousandths as Float or Double.
*>
*> Entry point:
*>   REGISTRY-PACKET-BUILD USING registry number (BINARY-LONG, standin §4.2 #), PB-BUFFER (appended
*>     to): the Registry Data packet (id + body), or nothing for an empty or unknown registry.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. REGISTRY-PACKET-BUILD.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY REGISTRY.
 01 WS-PACKET-ID           BINARY-LONG VALUE 7.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ENTRY               BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 L-NUMBER               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-NUMBER PB-BUFFER.
     IF L-NUMBER >= 0 AND L-NUMBER < REG-COUNT
         COMPUTE WS-ROW = L-NUMBER + 1
         IF RG-ENTRY-COUNT(WS-ROW) > 0
             CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-PACKET-ID
             CALL "PB-PUT-IDENTIFIER" USING PB-BUFFER RG-KEY(WS-ROW) RG-KEY-LENGTH(WS-ROW)
             CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER RG-ENTRY-COUNT(WS-ROW)
             PERFORM VARYING WS-ENTRY FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-ENTRY > RG-ENTRY-COUNT(WS-ROW)
                 EVALUATE RG-KIND(WS-ROW)
                     WHEN RGK-BIOME
                         CALL "REGISTRY-BIOME-ENTRY" USING WS-ENTRY PB-BUFFER
                     WHEN RGK-CHAT
                         CALL "REGISTRY-CHAT-ENTRY" USING WS-ENTRY PB-BUFFER
                     WHEN RGK-MV
                         CALL "REGISTRY-MV-ENTRY" USING RG-MV-ROW(WS-ROW) PB-BUFFER
                     WHEN RGK-DIMENSION-TYPE
                         CALL "REGISTRY-DIMTYPE-ENTRY" USING WS-ENTRY PB-BUFFER
                     WHEN RGK-DAMAGE
                         CALL "REGISTRY-DAMAGE-ENTRY" USING WS-ENTRY PB-BUFFER
                     WHEN OTHER
                         CALL "REGISTRY-CLOCK-ENTRY" USING WS-ENTRY PB-BUFFER
                 END-EVALUATE
             END-PERFORM
         END-IF
     END-IF
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM REGISTRY-PACKET-BUILD.

